row.cell:
100–120 sq. miles may need to be permanently removed for new bases;
                            little recurring public impact except for perceptions of dispersal
                            exercises.

Nominally assessed to have 70% survivability; significant endurance
                            problems if support bases and tactical warning systems are attacked;
                            spread/hide across very large number of airfields helps considerably;
                            ability to counter Soviet surveillance may be important.

Environmental objections—but may be less focused than for MAP, etc.;
                                wisdom of depending on strategic warning
                                will be continously questioned.
